  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nThe difference between compound interest and simple interest at 10% per annum for 2 years is Rs. 250.\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nSI = ((P × R × T))/(100)\n\nCI = P(1 + R%)T - P\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nAccording to the question,\n\n250 = CI - SI\n\n⇒ 250 = [P(1 + R%)T - P] - [((P × R × T))/(100)]\n\n⇒ 250 = P{[(1 + R%)T - 1] - [((R × T))/(100)]}\n\n⇒ 250 = P{[(1 + 10%)2 - 1] - [((10 × 2))/(100)]}\n\n⇒ 250 = P{[(1 + 0.10)2 - 1] - [(20)/(100)]}\n\n⇒ 250 = P{[(1.1)2 - 1] - [0.20]}\n\n⇒ 250 = P{[1.21 - 1] - 0.20}\n\n⇒ 250 = P{0.21 - 0.20}\n\n⇒ 250 = 0.01P\n\n⇒ P = (250)/(0.01) = Rs. 25000\n\n**∴ The sum is Rs. 25000.**\n\n89:T",
